# What a policy-finder instance's worktree holds: its sparse checkout
# (new_instance.sh, non-cone patterns in .gitignore syntax, later lines win).
# The agent learns the game from docs/reports/basics.md and arrives at
# everything about human and simulated behaviour itself, from the raw data and
# the reference sims: no reports, notes, plans or analyses of earlier work.

# the top-level files, but no folder, README.md or CLAUDE.md
/*
!/*/
!/README.md
!/CLAUDE.md

# the code, configs, models and data the agent and its sweep use
/.claude/
/src/
/configs/
/scripts/
!/scripts/data_analysis/
/artifacts/
/data/
/experiments/

# the game rules, and the reference sims the rule faces (experiment 2;
# experiment 1's, for an instance with setting exp1; exp2_multi's game doc,
# which names no governor: the export keeps the instance's own)
/docs/reports/basics.md
/plots/simulation/25_LEVIN_run1_ah_zero_pairings_batched/
/docs/reports/basics_exp1.md
/docs/reports/basics_exp2_multi.md
/plots/simulation/29_EXP1_reference/

# what the instance writes: its notes and its sweeps
/notes/policy_finder/
/plots/simulation/policy_finder/
